ScaleHLS
Copyright 2020-2021 The ScaleHLS Authors
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 with LLVM Exceptions
(licenses/ScaleHLS.txt)
https://github.com/UIUC-ChenLab/scalehls

The HLS/Dataflow dialect and parts of the analysis and lowering passes are adopted
from ScaleHLS, directly or through Stream-HLS (which records the same provenance in
its license/ScaleHLS.txt), and have since been modified and extended. Each of these
files carries the ScaleHLS notice:

  mlir/include/streamhls/Dialect/Dataflow/IR/Attributes.td
  mlir/include/streamhls/Dialect/Dataflow/IR/Dataflow.h
  mlir/include/streamhls/Dialect/Dataflow/IR/Dataflow.td
  mlir/include/streamhls/Dialect/Dataflow/IR/Interfaces.td
  mlir/include/streamhls/Dialect/Dataflow/IR/Ops.td
  mlir/include/streamhls/Dialect/Dataflow/IR/Types.td
  mlir/include/streamhls/Dialect/Dataflow/Transforms/Estimator.h
  mlir/include/streamhls/Dialect/Dataflow/Transforms/Passes.td (in part)
  mlir/include/streamhls/InitAllDialects.h
  mlir/include/streamhls/InitAllPasses.h
  mlir/lib/Dialect/Dataflow/Analysis/QoREstimation.cpp
  mlir/lib/Dialect/Dataflow/IR/Dataflow.cpp
  mlir/lib/Dialect/Dataflow/Transforms/LowerCopyToAffine.cpp
  mlir/lib/Dialect/Dataflow/Transforms/LowerSubviewToAffine.cpp
  mlir/lib/Dialect/Dataflow/Transforms/RemoveLoopsOfUnitIter.cpp

The HLS C++ emitters, visitor and support utilities listed under HeteroCL below
descend from ScaleHLS's emitter as well; their notices say "Modification: ScaleHLS".

ScaleHLS-HIDA (https://github.com/UIUC-ChenLab/ScaleHLS-HIDA) is developed from the
same code base under the same license. A line-level comparison against the full
histories of both repositories found no code specific to HIDA in ST-Flow.

